## 1. The 7-Stage Mobile Verification Ladder

In web engineering, deployment often finishes when a container starts serving HTTP traffic. In mobile engineering, distribution passes through a multi-tier cryptographic and store distribution pipeline before a single binary bit can execute on a tester's device.

Enterprise mobile teams monitor deployments through the **7-Stage Verification Ladder**:

<DiagramExpand id="diag-verification-ladder" title="The 7-Stage Mobile Verification Ladder">

```mermaid
graph TD
    classDef stage fill:#13251c,stroke:#22c55e,stroke-width:2px,color:#ffffff
    classDef error fill:#2d1515,stroke:#ef4444,stroke-width:2px,color:#ffffff

    S1["Stage 1: BuildStarted"] --> S2["Stage 2: BuildSuccessful"]
    S2 --> S3["Stage 3: ArtifactValidated"]
    S3 --> S4["Stage 4: Uploaded"]
    S4 --> S5["Stage 5: Signed"]
    S5 --> S6["Stage 6: Enabled"]
    S6 --> S7["Stage 7: UserVisible"]

    S1 -. "Env or SSH Failure" .-> E1["Abort: Infrastructure Failure"]
    S2 -. "Compilation or Lint Fail" .-> E2["Abort: Codebase Defect"]
    S3 -. "Invalid Keystore or Bundle ID" .-> E3["Abort: Packaging Defect"]
