## 3. Top 10 Mobile CI/CD Build Errors and 60-Second Fixes

The following battle-tested troubleshooting matrix covers 95% of all build failures encountered by React Native engineers on Bitrise.

### 1. Android NDK Architecture Mismatch
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>Execution failed for task ':react-native-reanimated:buildCMakeDebug[arm64-v8a]'. NDK at /opt/android-sdk/ndk/23.1.7779620 did not have a valid source.properties.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** Bitrise Android stack updated its default NDK version, while `android/app/build.gradle` requested an incompatible legacy version.
* **60-Second Fix:** Explicitly pin the NDK version in `android/app/build.gradle` matching the Bitrise system stack:
  ```groovy
  android {
      ndkVersion = "25.1.8937393" // Match Bitrise installed Android NDK
  }
  ```

---

### 2. CocoaPods Lockfile Out of Sync
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>[!] The sandbox is not in sync with the Podfile.lock. Run 'pod install' or update your CocoaPods installation.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** A developer updated `package.json` locally on their laptop, committed the change, but forgot to run `pod install` inside the `ios/` directory, causing a mismatch with `ios/Podfile.lock`.
* **60-Second Fix:** Run clean pod installation on your branch, commit the resulting `Podfile.lock`, and push:
  ```bash
  cd ios && rm -rf Pods Podfile.lock && pod install --repo-update && git commit -am "fix(ios): synchronize Podfile.lock" && git push
  ```

---

### 3. Gradle JVM Heap Out of Memory (OOM)
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>Expiring Daemon because JVM heap space is exhausted. java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: GC overhead limit exceeded.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** The default Gradle daemon allocation (1.5 GB) is insufficient for compiling large React Native multi-module codebases with R8 code shrinking enabled.
* **60-Second Fix:** Increase Gradle heap allocation in `android/gradle.properties`:
  ```properties
  org.gradle.jvmargs=-Xmx4096m -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=1024m -XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
  org.gradle.parallel=true
  org.gradle.caching=true
  ```

---

### 4. Apple Missing Distribution Certificate
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>Error: No signing certificate "Apple Distribution" found matching team ID "57246542" in keychain.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** Bitrise step `xcode-archive` executed without downloading or unlocking the code signing certificate, or the certificate expired.
* **60-Second Fix:** Ensure the `auto-provision-ios@3` step is positioned **immediately prior** to `xcode-archive@4` and uses valid `APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_P8` credentials.

---

### 5. Google Play API: 403 Forbidden
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>Google Play API: 403 Forbidden - The caller does not have permission for the requested project.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** The Google Cloud Service Account email has not been granted release permissions inside Google Play Console, or the initial release was never uploaded manually.
* **60-Second Fix:** Open Google Play Console &gt; **Users and permissions**, verify the service account email is listed under **Users**, and ensure the checkbox **Release apps to testing tracks** is checked.

---

### 6. Transporter 401 Unauthorized
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>[deliver] Transporter transfer failed. 401 Unauthorized: Invalid authentication token.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** The `APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_P8` secret stored in Bitrise contains trailing whitespace, has lost newline characters, or the App Store Connect Key was revoked.
* **60-Second Fix:** Open Bitrise **Secrets**, re-paste the full text of `AuthKey_*.p8` including the `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----` and `-----END PRIVATE KEY-----` headers, and verify that the Key ID matches the filename.

---

### 7. Gradle Wrapper Missing Execution Bit
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>bash: ./gradlew: Permission denied. Step failed with exit code 126.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** A developer on Windows committed `android/gradlew` without Unix executable permissions (`+x`).
* **60-Second Fix:** Update Git file permissions mode from your terminal:
  ```bash
  git update-index --chmod=+x android/gradlew
  git commit -m "fix(ci): grant execute permissions to android/gradlew"
  git push
  ```

---

### 8. Danger.js GitHub API Rate Limit Exceeded
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>Danger failed: Error: API rate limit exceeded for user ID (403 Forbidden).</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** The `DANGER_GITHUB_API_TOKEN` environment variable was empty or missing, forcing Danger to make unauthenticated requests subject to GitHub's 60 req/hr IP rate limit.
* **60-Second Fix:** Generate a fine-grained GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT) with `pull_requests: write` permissions and assign it to `DANGER_GITHUB_API_TOKEN` in Bitrise Secrets.

---

### 9. TestFlight Missing Export Compliance
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>TestFlight build status: Missing Compliance. Testing cannot begin until encryption information is provided.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** Apple requires apps using standard HTTPS encryption to declare exemption status in `Info.plist`. Without this, builds halt waiting for human web console clicks.
* **60-Second Fix:** Insert the compliance key into `ios/MobileApp/Info.plist`:
  ```xml
  <key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
  <false/>
  ```

---

### 10. Yarn Frozen Lockfile Assertion Failure
<div class="portal-alert-box warning">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">SYMPTOM</div>
  <p><code>error Your lockfile needs to be updated, but --frozen-lockfile was specified.</code></p>
</div>

* **Root Cause:** Dependencies in `package.json` were modified manually in an editor without running `yarn install` locally to update `yarn.lock`.
* **60-Second Fix:** Run `yarn install` locally, commit the synchronized `yarn.lock`, and push to your PR branch:
  ```bash
  yarn install
  git commit -am "fix: synchronize yarn.lock with package.json"
  git push
  ```

